{
  "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
  "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KRETZER: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nThe nature and logic of Martinez naturally\napplies to claims of ineffective assistance of appellate\ncounsel, just as it does to claims of ineffective\nassistance of trial counsel.\nErick Davila faces execution despite having\nbeen convicted pursuant to erroneous jury instructions\nthat vitiated his only viable defense. On direct\nappeal, Davila's counsel recognized the centrality of\nthe intent issue, but challenged only sufficiency of the\nevidence --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: May I ask you, when do\nyou believe that counsel below objected? And your brief\nseems to assume he did, but as I read the transcript, I\ncan't find where he objected clearly."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Given plain error\nreview, if there was no objection, wasn't the\nsufficiency of the evidence the best way to approach a\nforfeited error?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I mean, if you have\nsix issues that you think you can argue credibly before\nthe -- before the appellate court, you may decide it\nwould be much better to focus that court on the two or\nthree strongest issues, that adding the others will, in\nfact, dilute from the value of that.\nSo when you have these -- I'm not talking\nabout this particular case. But in general, when you\nhave the claim of ineffective assistance of appellate\ncounsel, it's sometimes easy in retrospect to say, well,\nhere's an issue that, you know, maybe -- the appellate\ncounsel, in the exercise of discretion, thought it was\nlike number 6 in the order of -- of strength."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, on the -- on the\nissue of whether or not Martinez should be extended to\nalleged inadequate assistance of counsel on appeal, what\nis the test that I'm supposed to apply? The -- the\npracticality of this? The consequences? The private\ninterests of the prisoners and the public interest\nin finality -- is that what I'm supposed -- is there\nsome test you want me to apply?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, you're not\ndealing with the question asked."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0000-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: What concerns me about your\nposition is that it seems to blast an enormous hole in\nthe doctrine of procedural default."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0000-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Say, so what -- you started\nto say this, but I guess Martinez itself, one of the\nconcerns was that any mistake that the trial -- that the\ntrial attorney makes -- and normally, by the way, you --\nyou don't make ineffective assistance counsel claims on\ndirect appeal, I don't think."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What I -- I asked you really, is there any empirical information? Because, of course, I think you probably think no. But the other side may think yes. And so that's what I would like to know, is there any -- anyplace I could look to find out whether it has proved to be a burden or not, where there have been a lot of claims or not?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Criminal Justice Legal Foundation",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0001-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would also point the Court to the amicus brief for the Criminal Justice Legal Foundation at page 20. What it did was it looked at the last ten cases in the Ninth Circuit out of Arizona in capital cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But in -- in most States it does apply; isn't that right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Keller",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL KELLER: But Martinez focused on the fact that there was a particular trial error and a particular type of trial error that was not being able to be raised."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Keller",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL KELLER: But under that reasoning, it would be -- the right to counsel necessarily has to end at some point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Keller",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0002-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Extending an exception like this to an acknowledged set of claims that have an infinitesimally small chance of merit, that is not a good use of judicial resources."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: General, could I just -- I guess I got a little bit confused in your exchange with Justice Alito, because you had been pressing this is just going to be an infinitesimally small -- infinitesimally small, I think that that was your phrase."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Davila",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think there's serious pause, because all that Mr. Davila is asking is for the same standard as that which exists in Martinez."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0003-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The number of Federal courts actually having merits hearings on Strickland claims is incredibly small."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 0.6,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0003-0002",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Federal habeas is designed to prevent and correct severe malfunctions of the State trial system, that's probably a very good thing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 0.6,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0003-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "strategically try not to raise a claim here, so that, in fact, they can get some more favorable forum later on."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2016-16-6219",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "363b1ea8b1f03be4a9417e5081909e67a567dd275f4cdd2a4d23e056908bf3c5",
      "evidence_id": "ev-363b1ea8b1f0-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "above-entitled matter was submitted.) Alderson Reporting Company"
    },
